{"number":1194,"title":"Dashboard: pack-contributed metrics — design the extensibility contract","body":"The dashboard&#39;s panels are all owned by the `claudinite-dashboard` pack itself. Packs know facts about a repo that the dashboard cannot: a release pack knows the last release, `executable-requirements` knows which requirements moved, the canon knows which packs are new. Nothing lets a pack surface its own key metrics on the repo page or the fleet page.

Design the contract by which any pack contributes metrics to the dashboard — declarative, cheap under the page&#39;s budget policy, safe to render (no pack code in the page), version-tolerant, with distinct shapes for the fleet view and the repo view.

Deliverable: `docs/dashboard-pack-metrics/DESIGN.md` — the end state, its rationale, and the alternatives with their drawbacks. Implementation is follow-up work, not this issue.","state":"open","html_url":"https://github.com/missingbulb/Claudinite/issues/1194","user":{"login":"missingbulb","id":73882448,"profile_url":"https://github.com/missingbulb","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/73882448?v=4"},"author_association":"OWNER","assignees":[],"reactions":{"total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"hooray":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"created_at":"2026-08-21T20:20:41Z","updated_at":"2026-08-21T20:20:41Z","has_parent":false,"has_children":false,"closed_by_pull_requests":{"total_count":1,"references":[{"number":1195,"title":"Design pack-contributed dashboard metrics","state":"OPEN","url":"https://github.com/missingbulb/Claudinite/pull/1195","repository":"missingbulb/Claudinite"}]}}

{"number":722,"title":"Align the website repos&#39; release flows on one github-pages-serving standard","body":"EdFringeNow, ClaudiniteWebsite and MissingBulbWebsite each hand-roll the same GitHub Pages release flow with local drift (copied `bump-version.mjs`, deploy-on-every-push, analytics-token injection, no tags or releases). The canon `static-website` pack (#611) owns this territory but has zero adopters; MissingBulbWebsite&#39;s adoption attempt (its PR #39) is stalled on the disapproved #626.

Task: compare the three flows, analyze whether the consolidation policy/process is sound, and design the corrections — eliminating the bespoke mechanisms into a Claudinite pack, minimizing GitHub Actions surface (logic in the vendored engine where no secret/token forces Actions) and minimizing manual repo-settings changes, while keeping the flow customizable per repo. Acceptance probe: purge all release aspects and settings from MissingBulbWebsite so it simulates a fresh repo, adopt the pack, and the first release works on the first go.

Deliverables on this branch: `docs/website-release-flows/COMPARISON.md` and `DESIGN.md`.","state":"open","html_url":"https://github.com/missingbulb/Claudinite/issues/722","user":{"login":"missingbulb","id":73882448,"profile_url":"https://github.com/missingbulb","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/73882448?v=4"},"author_association":"OWNER","labels":["needs-decision"],"assignees":[],"comments":3,"reactions":{"total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"hooray":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"created_at":"2026-08-09T10:16:02Z","updated_at":"2026-08-20T05:23:05Z","has_parent":false,"has_children":false,"closed_by_pull_requests":{"total_count":0,"references":[]}}

{"number":334,"title":"DESIGN.md trade-offs: delivery mode is now a security knob; name the vendored mount&#39;s supply-chain improvement","body":"From a design review of `mount/DESIGN.md` (#315). Doc-only.

**The improvement (worth recording as a design benefit):** the vendored mount closes a real supply-chain exposure — consumers previously executed an unauthenticated, unpinned `codeload` tarball at every session start *and on every Bash call* (the PreToolUse guard). Post-flip, consumers execute only code committed in their own history: diffs reviewable, rollback = revert the nightly&#39;s commit.

**The residual (worth a sentence in §10):** for `push`-delivery members, the nightly is an unreviewed fleet-wide code-write channel into `main`; `pr` delivery buys a human review gate on the entire supply chain. That makes `maintenance.delivery` a **security decision**, not just a workflow preference — a member holding secrets or deploy credentials may reasonably choose `pr` for that reason alone. (The preferences fetch remains the one session-time fetch: fail-soft prose, not executed code — acceptable residue, worth naming as such.)","state":"open","html_url":"https://github.com/missingbulb/Claudinite/issues/334","user":{"login":"missingbulb","id":73882448,"profile_url":"https://github.com/missingbulb","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/73882448?v=4"},"author_association":"OWNER","labels":["quick-win"],"assignees":[],"comments":5,"reactions":{"total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"hooray":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"created_at":"2026-07-18T19:49:54Z","updated_at":"2026-08-19T05:18:55Z","has_parent":false,"has_children":false,"closed_by_pull_requests":{"total_count":0,"references":[]}}

