1	// The usage fold's THIRD source: what each scheduled occurrence actually came to.
2	//
3	// The slot scheduler used to print that per due task into its own Actions log, and the
4	// fold counted those lines. That writer retired with the slot scheduler (#974) and the
5	// queue does not print an equivalent — because it does not need to. Every occurrence
6	// is a work ITEM, and when it converges it closes wearing an `outcome:*` label. The
7	// record is better than the log line was (it survives Actions retention, it is
8	// clickable, and it carries the task on its own title) and it is a different read,
9	// which is what #994 asked for. This module is that read.
10	//
11	// APPEND-ONCE past `queueFoldedThrough`, for the same reason the run listing is
12	// forward-only: this is a paged REST resource where the capture files are local git.
13	// It is safe to append rather than recompute because a CLOSED item is settled — the
14	// outcome label is written at convergence and nothing later moves it — so an item is
15	// counted on the one fold that first sees it closed and never again.
16	//
17	// The boundary is `closed_at`, not `updated_at`: the listing is asked for everything
18	// touched since the mark (a comment on an old item counts as a touch), and only items
19	// that closed past the mark are counted. Closing happens in real time, so the mark is
20	// monotone and the filter is exactly-once.
21	//
22	// FAIL-SOFT, like every other source here: an unreadable listing costs the queue rows
23	// this run and leaves the mark where it was.
24	
